repository-code: https://github.com/zlvm/contextual_individuation_toolkit
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: |-
  First stable release, archived for citation and auditing alongside its companion manuscript, "Technical Manual for a Toolkit for Measuring Contextual Individuation in Transformer Language Models".

  Contents:
  - contextual_individuation.ipynb: the full pipeline (bridge-form declaration, Wikipedia corpus acquisition, occurrence localization, layer-wise representation extraction, pairwise silhouette measurement, and paired PCA visualization).
  - requirements.txt: pinned dependency versions for local reproducibility.
  - .env.example: template for the contact-email variable used in the Wikipedia API User-Agent header.

  License: CC BY 4.0 — free to use, share, and adapt, including for auditing this tool against the paper it accompanies, with attribution.

  Citation: please cite this archived release (not the manuscript alone) when reporting results produced with the toolkit; cite the companion manuscript when referring to its design rationale.

  Hosting institutions: Universidade Estadual de Campinas (UNICAMP); Centro de Pesquisa em Mobilidade Elétrica (CEMOBE) / Laboratórios em Eletrônica de Potência (LEPO); Centro de Estudos de Energia e Petróleo (CEPETRO); Centro de Lógica, Epistemologia e História da Ciência (CLE).
